# Deliberate differences (pennmush-compatibility.md, #1134) that need a second player, God or a server
# setting to show, so the profile cannot give them a one-line ```sharp example. Each case is the example
# for one **A choice.** entry and names it; the one step that shows the difference is allowlisted in
# known-differences.json under that entry's heading, and every other step has to match or be an open gap.
# Configuration is changed only inside a case and put back before it ends.

::case choice.housekeeping  PennMUSH's file and allocator housekeeping answers NOT SUPPORTED
::login god One godpass
::as god
@stats/chunks
@logwipe/check wrongpassword

::case choice.dropto  a drop-to move's event names who caused it
# A STICKY room keeps what is dropped in it until the last player leaves, then sends it to its drop-to
# (send_contents, move.c:187): that move is the one PennMUSH reports as caused by SYSEVENT. The handler
# records the enactor of that move only, so the step that shows it holds nothing else. EventSink digs the
# room, so dig()'s "created with room number" goes to it, not to a transcript: PennMUSH reuses a slot freed
# by an earlier scenario, and that deliberate difference is not what this case shows.
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
::as wiz
@power me=No_Pay
think [set(me,HOMELOC:[loc(me)])][set(me,OLDEVENTS:[config(event_handler)])]
@create EventSink
&MKROOM EventSink=think [set(me,DROPROOM:[dig(DropRoom)])]
@trigger EventSink/MKROOM
::settle
&OBJECT`MOVE EventSink=@switch %4=dropto,{&DROPTO_BY me=%#}
::as god
@config/set event_handler=[locate(*Wiz,EventSink,i)]
::as wiz
@link [get(EventSink/DROPROOM)]=[loc(*Alice)]
@set [get(EventSink/DROPROOM)]=STICKY
@create Pebble
@tel me=[get(EventSink/DROPROOM)]
drop Pebble
@tel me=[v(HOMELOC)]
::settle
think [get(EventSink/DROPTO_BY)]
::as god
@config/set event_handler=[if(get(*Wiz/OLDEVENTS),get(*Wiz/OLDEVENTS),-1)]

::case choice.mail-fwd  a refused forward is reported
::login alice Alice alicepass
::login bob Bob bobpass
::as bob
@lock/mail me=!*Alice
::as alice
@mail Alice=Forward me/A note to pass on.
@mail/fwd 1=*Bob
::as bob
@unlock/mail me

::case choice.mail-folder  folders are named freely and created on delivery
::as bob
&MAILFILTER me=newbox
::as alice
@mail Bob=Filed/Where does this go?
::as bob
&MAILFILTER me

::case choice.mail-forwardlist  an empty MAILFORWARDLIST is no list
::as bob
&MAILFORWARDLIST me=
think [hasattr(me,MAILFORWARDLIST)]
::as alice
@mail Bob=Listed/Does this arrive?
::as bob
&MAILFORWARDLIST me

::case choice.restrictions-reapply  changing command_restrictions starts its commands again
# PennMUSH applies each restrict_command line once (conf.c:866-896), so the @command/restrict after it
# stands. SharpMUSH keeps the lines as command_restrictions and applies the whole setting again when it
# changes, so @find goes back to the wizard-only line. @dump is WIZARD-locked on both servers already.
::as god
@config/set restrict_command=@find wizard
@command/restrict @find=!FLAG^GAGGED
@config/set restrict_command=@dump wizard
::as alice
@find Widget
::as god
@command/restrict @find=!FLAG^GAGGED
